---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CTABand from '@/components/CTABand.astro';
import PageHero from '@/components/PageHero.astro';

const planningServices = [
  {
    name: 'Retirement Income Planning',
    href: '/retirement-income-planning/',
    desc: 'Turning what you have saved into income that lasts, while managing withdrawals, taxes, and the years when markets do not cooperate.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Estate Planning',
    href: '/financial-services/estate-planning/',
    desc: 'Organizing the financial side of your legacy so your executor has a clear roadmap, your beneficiary designations line up with your will, and less goes to tax than it otherwise would.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Charitable Giving',
    href: '/charitable-giving/',
    desc: 'Structuring donations of cash, securities, life insurance, or a donor advised fund so the causes you support get more, and your estate pays less.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Financial Planning | Heidi Blondin Financial"
  description="Retirement income, estate, and charitable giving planning for Ontario families. Independent, plain language advice from a Certified Financial Planner in Kingston."
>

  <PageHero title="Planning"
    center
  />

  <section class="bg-white section-gap">
    <div class="container-content max-w-3xl">
      <div class="font-sans text-[17px] text-brand-ink/75 leading-relaxed space-y-4">
        <p>Most people arrive with the pieces already in hand: a will drafted years ago, savings in two or three places, a pension statement they have never really read. What is missing is the part that connects them.</p>
        <p>That is the work. For some clients it starts with retirement income, because a date has been set and the paycheque is about to stop. For others the estate comes first, often after watching someone else's get settled badly. Giving tends to come up later, once the rest is steady.</p>
        <p>We are independent, so none of this begins with a product. We listen first, build the plan around what you actually want, and choose the tools last. Heidi Blondin is a Certified Financial Planner, working with a team that handles the follow through: paperwork, transactions, and the questions that come up between meetings.</p>
        <p>Each of these areas has its own page, with more detail on what is involved:</p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-3">
        {planningServices.map(item => (
          <a href={item.href} class="group block border border-brand-plum/10 px-6 py-5 hover:border-brand-plum/25 hover:shadow-sm transition-all">
            <span class="flex items-center gap-3">
              <span class="flex-1 font-sans text-sm font-semibold text-brand-plum group-hover:text-brand-goldDark transition-colors">{item.name}</span>
              <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-brand-gold flex-shrink-0 group-hover:translate-x-0.5 transition-transform" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M13.5 4.5 21 12m0 0-7.5 7.5M21 12H3"/></svg>
            </span>
            <span class="mt-2 block font-sans text-[15px] text-brand-ink/70 leading-relaxed">{item.desc}</span>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-h2 text-brand-plum mb-4">Where Planning Usually Starts</h2>
        <div class="font-sans text-[17px] text-brand-ink/75 leading-relaxed space-y-4">
          <p>A first meeting is mostly listening. We want to know what you are saving for, who depends on you, and what would go wrong tomorrow if something happened to you. Nothing gets recommended in that meeting.</p>
          <p>From there we look at what you already have in place and where the gaps are. Sometimes the answer is straightforward, like a beneficiary designation that no longer matches the will it was meant to support. Sometimes it takes longer, because retirement income, tax, and estate decisions pull on each other and changing one moves the others.</p>
          <p>You will get the reasoning in plain language, not a binder you never open. If a recommendation does not make sense to you, we have not finished explaining it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 bg-brand-tintPlum border-l-4 border-brand-plum/40 p-8">
        <blockquote class="font-sans text-[15px] text-brand-ink/75 italic leading-relaxed">"Heidi Blondin Financial has skillfully managed our retirement investments and finances for years. Recently we have also consulted regarding wills and estate planning. Advice is always realistic, honest, and informative. Heidi and her team are professional, approachable, and accessible. Angela is a delightful liaison and document wizard. They keep our accounts current and competitive in this roller coaster world. Personally, Blondin Financial gives us peace of mind, which adds so much to our quality of life."</blockquote>
        <p class="mt-4 font-sans text-xs font-semibold text-brand-plum/70">Angela M.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 bg-brand-tintPlum p-5 border-l-2 border-brand-plum/30">
        <p class="font-sans text-xs text-brand-ink/70 leading-relaxed">This page is for general information purposes only and does not constitute personalized financial, legal, or tax advice. Estate planning often involves legal documents (wills, powers of attorney) that require a qualified estate lawyer. We work alongside your legal advisor as part of an integrated planning team.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTABand heading="Let's talk about your plan" sub="Book a free consultation. We will listen first and tell you honestly whether we can help." />

</BaseLayout>
